    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, what can an elephant's trunk do?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "🐘",
          "label": "Elephant"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "👃",
          "label": "Trunk?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "So much! A trunk is a nose and an upper lip, joined together into one long, strong tube.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐘",
        "text": "Nose + lip = trunk",
        "cue": "nose",
        "sub": "Long and strong",
        "sub_cue": "strong"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So it smells with it?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Elephants are amazing smellers. They can sniff out food and water from far away.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "👃",
        "text": "A super sniffer",
        "cue": "sniff",
        "sub": "Food and water, far away",
        "sub_cue": "far"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Do they drink through it, like a straw?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not quite! They suck water up into the trunk, then squirt it into their mouths.",
      "punch": "squirt",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Trunk drink",
        "traveler": "💧",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🌊",
            "label": "Suck up water",
            "cue": "suck"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🐘",
            "label": "In the trunk",
            "cue": "trunk"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💦",
            "label": "Squirt!",
            "cue": "squirt"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👄",
            "label": "Into mouth",
            "cue": "mouths"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They also spray water to take a shower, or toss dust on their backs, like sunscreen!",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Spray time",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🚿",
            "label": "Shower",
            "cue": "shower"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "label": "Dust bath",
            "cue": "dust"
          },
          {
            "icon": "☀️",
            "label": "Like sunscreen",
            "cue": "sunscreen"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Can it pick things up?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! A trunk can grab something as small as a single leaf, or as heavy as a big log.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌿",
        "text": "Grabs small and big",
        "cue": "grab",
        "sub": "A leaf or a log!",
        "sub_cue": "log"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What else can it do?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Elephants use their trunks to say hello, hug their babies, and make loud trumpet sounds!",
      "board": {
        "type": "gallery",
        "title": "Trunk talk",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "👋",
            "label": "Say hello",
            "cue": "hello"
